VEN`. No other changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 379139, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01TV8g2XnnjMYHse7J15pajR", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379139, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TV8g2XnnjMYHse7J15pajR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383074, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` said in its comment that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually rounded halves up. So `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't have it, so it's probably an internal finance spec. Both the code comment and the test call for banker's rounding, so I went with that.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TCdrGzFLSre7zUh2wQ9KHb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XeP