": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Opening the PR now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TV8g2XnnjMYHse7J15pajR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the failing nightly build.\n\n`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed (`2.665` rounded to `2.67` instead of `2.66`).\n\nChange: switch the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` said in its comment that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually rounded halves up. So `2.665` became `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't have it, so it's probably an internal finance spec. Both the code comment and the test call for banker's rounding, so I went with that.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}